From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 10:05:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: msm8998 needs the two MMSS NoC clocks

The msm8998 venus support was added as an RFC "based on similar msm8996
code" and, by the author's own framing, never proven on hardware. On a
Pixel 2 XL it takes the SoC down below printk, and the bisect lands on a
single write: 0x00000003 to base+0x80124, the first VBIF register, from
venus_set_registers(). Skipping the preset table avoids the wedge entirely.

VBIF is the venus-to-MMSS-NoC bridge, so that write is the first thing to
need a clocked path out of the block -- and one of the clocks it needs is
not running. On a booted device with the display active:

  gcc_mmss_sys_noc_axi_clk    enable_count 0   rate 0
  mnoc_ahb_clk                enable_count 2   rate 40000000

Nothing else in the system votes the MMSS system NoC AXI clock, while
mnoc_ahb_clk happens to be on because the display uses it. That is exactly
the asymmetry observed: the AHB config path works -- every CPU write to the
venus wrapper lands -- and the AXI data path through VBIF does not.

The vendor devicetree agrees. Its pil-tz venus node lists six clocks and
holds all six as proxy clocks across firmware authentication:

  clock-names = "core_clk", "mnoc_ahb_clk", "iface_clk",
                "noc_axi_clk", "bus_clk", "maxi_clk"

Mainline carries four of them. Add the missing two, and raise
VIDC_CLKS_NUM_MAX to fit, which no other platform's count exceeds.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi    |  7 +++++--
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++--
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.h |  2 +-
 3 files changed, 23 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi
index c237a1210abe..7caea30bdaa9 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi
@@ -4236,8 +4236,11 @@ venus: video-codec@cc00000 {
 			clocks = <&mmcc VIDEO_CORE_CLK>,
 				 <&mmcc VIDEO_AHB_CLK>,
 				 <&mmcc VIDEO_AXI_CLK>,
-				 <&mmcc VIDEO_MAXI_CLK>;
-			clock-names = "core", "iface", "bus", "mbus";
+				 <&mmcc VIDEO_MAXI_CLK>,
+				 <&mmcc MNOC_AHB_CLK>,
+				 <&gcc GCC_MMSS_SYS_NOC_AXI_CLK>;
+			clock-names = "core", "iface", "bus", "mbus",
+				      "mnoc_ahb", "noc_axi";
 			iommus = <&mmss_smmu 0x400>,
 				 <&mmss_smmu 0x401>,
 				 <&mmss_smmu 0x40a>,
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
index 7a3b16b621ac..9a744420763d 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
@@ -858,8 +858,23 @@ static const struct venus_resources msm8998_res = {
 	.freq_tbl_size = ARRAY_SIZE(msm8998_freq_table),
 	.reg_tbl = msm8998_reg_preset,
 	.reg_tbl_size = ARRAY_SIZE(msm8998_reg_preset),
-	.clks = { "core", "iface", "bus", "mbus" },
-	.clks_num = 4,
+	/*
+	 * The two NoC clocks are not optional here, whatever msm8996 got away
+	 * with. VBIF is the venus-to-MMSS-NoC bridge, and the first write into
+	 * it -- 0x80124, from venus_set_registers() -- hangs the fabric hard
+	 * enough that only the watchdog recovers. gcc_mmss_sys_noc_axi_clk is
+	 * measurably OFF (enable_count 0, rate 0) on a booted msm8998 with the
+	 * display up, because nothing else votes it; mnoc_ahb_clk happens to be
+	 * on from the display, which is why the AHB config path works while the
+	 * AXI data path does not.
+	 *
+	 * The vendor agrees: its pil-tz venus node lists six clocks, and holds
+	 * all six as proxy clocks across firmware authentication --
+	 *   "core_clk", "mnoc_ahb_clk", "iface_clk",
+	 *   "noc_axi_clk", "bus_clk", "maxi_clk"
+	 */
+	.clks = { "core", "iface", "bus", "mbus", "mnoc_ahb", "noc_axi" },
+	.clks_num = 6,
 	.vcodec0_clks = { "core" },
 	.vcodec1_clks = { "core" },
 	.vcodec_clks_num = 1,
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.h b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.h
index 46705a666776..1fff66db14b3 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.h
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@
 #define VDBGH	"VenusHigh: "
 #define VDBGFW	"VenusFW  : "
 
-#define VIDC_CLKS_NUM_MAX		4
+#define VIDC_CLKS_NUM_MAX		6
 #define VIDC_VCODEC_CLKS_NUM_MAX	2
 #define VIDC_RESETS_NUM_MAX		2
 #define VIDC_MAX_HIER_CODING_LAYER 6
